{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39824",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Invoking integer overflow in NewNTUnicodeString in golang.org/x/sys/windows"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "NewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39824",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39824\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/sys\nFixed Version: 0.44.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-39824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39824)\nNewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39824**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/sys|0.44.0|[CVE-2026-39824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39824)|\n\nNewNTUnicodeString does not check for string length overflow. When provided with a string that overflows the maximum size of a NTUnicodeString (a 16-bit number of bytes), it returns a truncated string rather than an error."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39822",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symli ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39822\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: stdlib\nFixed Version: 1.25.12, 1.26.5, 1.27.0-rc.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-39822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822)\nOn Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39822**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|stdlib|1.25.12, 1.26.5, 1.27.0-rc.2|[CVE-2026-39822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39822)|\n\nOn Unix systems, opening a file in an os.Root improperly follows symlinks to locations outside of the Root when the final path component of the a path is a symbolic link and the path ends in /. For example, 'root.Open(\"symlink/\")' will open \"symlink\" even when \"symlink\" is a symbolic link pointing outside of the root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "UNKNOWN"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of Service due to Panic in AWS SDK for Go v2 SDK EventStream Decoder"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "**CVSSv3.1 Rating**: [Medium]\n**CVSSv3.1 Score**: [5.9]\n**CVSSv3.1 Vector String**: [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]\n\n## Summary and Impact\nAn issue exists in the the EventStream header decoder in AWS SDK for Go v2 in versions predating [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23). An actor can send a malformed EventStream response frame containing a crafted header value type byte outside the valid range, which can cause the host process to terminate.\n\nImpacted versions: \u003c [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23)\n\n## Patches\nThis issue has been addressed in versions [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23) and above. We recommend upgrading to the latest version and ensuring any forked or derivative code is patched to incorporate the new fixes. \n\n## Workarounds\nNot Applicable\n\n## References\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, we ask that you contact [AWS/Amazon] Security via our [vulnerability reporting page](https://aws.amazon.com/security/vulnerability-reporting) or directly via email to [aws-security@amazon.com](mailto:aws-security@amazon.com). Please do not create a public GitHub issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/s3\nFixed Version: 1.97.3\nLink: [GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2)\n**CVSSv3.1 Rating**: [Medium]\n**CVSSv3.1 Score**: [5.9]\n**CVSSv3.1 Vector String**: [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]\n\n## Summary and Impact\nAn issue exists in the the EventStream header decoder in AWS SDK for Go v2 in versions predating [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23). An actor can send a malformed EventStream response frame containing a crafted header value type byte outside the valid range, which can cause the host process to terminate.\n\nImpacted versions: \u003c [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23)\n\n## Patches\nThis issue has been addressed in versions [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23) and above. We recommend upgrading to the latest version and ensuring any forked or derivative code is patched to incorporate the new fixes. \n\n## Workarounds\nNot Applicable\n\n## References\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, we ask that you contact [AWS/Amazon] Security via our [vulnerability reporting page](https://aws.amazon.com/security/vulnerability-reporting) or directly via email to [aws-security@amazon.com](mailto:aws-security@amazon.com). Please do not create a public GitHub issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/s3|1.97.3|[GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2)|\n\n**CVSSv3.1 Rating**: [Medium]\n**CVSSv3.1 Score**: [5.9]\n**CVSSv3.1 Vector String**: [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]\n\n## Summary and Impact\nAn issue exists in the the EventStream header decoder in AWS SDK for Go v2 in versions predating [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23). An actor can send a malformed EventStream response frame containing a crafted header value type byte outside the valid range, which can cause the host process to terminate.\n\nImpacted versions: \u003c [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23)\n\n## Patches\nThis issue has been addressed in versions [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23) and above. We recommend upgrading to the latest version and ensuring any forked or derivative code is patched to incorporate the new fixes. \n\n## Workarounds\nNot Applicable\n\n## References\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, we ask that you contact [AWS/Amazon] Security via our [vulnerability reporting page](https://aws.amazon.com/security/vulnerability-reporting) or directly via email to [aws-security@amazon.com](mailto:aws-security@amazon.com). Please do not create a public GitHub issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.9,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-10543",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "paho.mqtt.golang: paho.mqtt.golang: Integer Overflow in UTF-8 String Encoding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In Eclipse Paho Go MQTT v3.1 library (paho.mqtt.golang) versions \u003c=1.5.0 UTF-8 encoded strings, passed into the library, may be incorrectly encoded if their length exceeds 65535 bytes. This may lead to unexpected content in packets sent to the server (for example, part of an MQTT topic may leak into the message body in a PUBLISH packet).\n\n\nThe issue arises because the length of the data passed in was converted from an int64/int32 (depending upon CPU) to an int16 without checks for overflows. The int16 length was then written, followed by the data (e.g. topic). This meant that when the data (e.g. topic) was over 65535 bytes then the amount of data written exceeds what the length field indicates. This could lead to a corrupt packet, or mean that the excess data leaks into another field (e.g. topic leaks into message body)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-10543",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-10543\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/eclipse/paho.mqtt.golang\nFixed Version: 1.5.1\nLink: [CVE-2025-10543](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-10543)\nIn Eclipse Paho Go MQTT v3.1 library (paho.mqtt.golang) versions \u003c=1.5.0 UTF-8 encoded strings, passed into the library, may be incorrectly encoded if their length exceeds 65535 bytes. This may lead to unexpected content in packets sent to the server (for example, part of an MQTT topic may leak into the message body in a PUBLISH packet).\n\n\nThe issue arises because the length of the data passed in was converted from an int64/int32 (depending upon CPU) to an int16 without checks for overflows. The int16 length was then written, followed by the data (e.g. topic). This meant that when the data (e.g. topic) was over 65535 bytes then the amount of data written exceeds what the length field indicates. This could lead to a corrupt packet, or mean that the excess data leaks into another field (e.g. topic leaks into message body).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-10543**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/eclipse/paho.mqtt.golang|1.5.1|[CVE-2025-10543](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-10543)|\n\nIn Eclipse Paho Go MQTT v3.1 library (paho.mqtt.golang) versions \u003c=1.5.0 UTF-8 encoded strings, passed into the library, may be incorrectly encoded if their length exceeds 65535 bytes. This may lead to unexpected content in packets sent to the server (for example, part of an MQTT topic may leak into the message body in a PUBLISH packet).\n\n\nThe issue arises because the length of the data passed in was converted from an int64/int32 (depending upon CPU) to an int16 without checks for overflows. The int16 length was then written, followed by the data (e.g. topic). This meant that when the data (e.g. topic) was over 65535 bytes then the amount of data written exceeds what the length field indicates. This could lead to a corrupt packet, or mean that the excess data leaks into another field (e.g. topic leaks into message body)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-40179",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus has Stored XSS via metric names and label values in Prometheus web UI tooltips and metrics explorer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. Versions 3.0 through 3.5.1 and 3.6.0 through 3.11.1 have stored cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in multiple components of the Prometheus web UI where metric names and label values are injected into innerHTML without escaping. In both the Mantine UI and old React UI, chart tooltips on the Graph page render metric names containing HTML/JavaScript without sanitization. In the old React UI, the Metric Explorer fuzzy search results use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without escaping, and heatmap cell tooltips interpolate le label values without sanitization. With Prometheus v3.x defaulting to UTF-8 metric and label name validation, characters like \u003c, \u003e, and \" are now valid in metric names and labels. An attacker who can inject metrics via a compromised scrape target, remote write, or OTLP receiver endpoint can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the Graph UI, potentially enabling configuration exfiltration, data deletion, or Prometheus shutdown depending on enabled flags. This issue has been fixed in versions 3.5.2 and 3.11.2. If developers are unable to immediately update, the following workarounds are recommended: ensure that the remote write receiver (--web.enable-remote-write-receiver) and the OTLP receiver (--web.enable-otlp-receiver) are not exposed to untrusted sources; verify that all scrape targets are trusted and not under attacker control; avoid enabling admin or mutating API endpoints (e.g., --web.enable-admin-api or --web.enable-lifecycle) in environments where untrusted data may be ingested; and refrain from clicking untrusted links, particularly those containing functions such as label_replace, as they may generate poisoned label names and values."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40179",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-40179\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/prometheus/prometheus\nFixed Version: 0.311.2-0.20260410083055-07c6232d159b\nLink: [CVE-2026-40179](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40179)\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. Versions 3.0 through 3.5.1 and 3.6.0 through 3.11.1 have stored cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in multiple components of the Prometheus web UI where metric names and label values are injected into innerHTML without escaping. In both the Mantine UI and old React UI, chart tooltips on the Graph page render metric names containing HTML/JavaScript without sanitization. In the old React UI, the Metric Explorer fuzzy search results use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without escaping, and heatmap cell tooltips interpolate le label values without sanitization. With Prometheus v3.x defaulting to UTF-8 metric and label name validation, characters like \u003c, \u003e, and \" are now valid in metric names and labels. An attacker who can inject metrics via a compromised scrape target, remote write, or OTLP receiver endpoint can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the Graph UI, potentially enabling configuration exfiltration, data deletion, or Prometheus shutdown depending on enabled flags. This issue has been fixed in versions 3.5.2 and 3.11.2. If developers are unable to immediately update, the following workarounds are recommended: ensure that the remote write receiver (--web.enable-remote-write-receiver) and the OTLP receiver (--web.enable-otlp-receiver) are not exposed to untrusted sources; verify that all scrape targets are trusted and not under attacker control; avoid enabling admin or mutating API endpoints (e.g., --web.enable-admin-api or --web.enable-lifecycle) in environments where untrusted data may be ingested; and refrain from clicking untrusted links, particularly those containing functions such as label_replace, as they may generate poisoned label names and values.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-40179**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/prometheus/prometheus|0.311.2-0.20260410083055-07c6232d159b|[CVE-2026-40179](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40179)|\n\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. Versions 3.0 through 3.5.1 and 3.6.0 through 3.11.1 have stored cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in multiple components of the Prometheus web UI where metric names and label values are injected into innerHTML without escaping. In both the Mantine UI and old React UI, chart tooltips on the Graph page render metric names containing HTML/JavaScript without sanitization. In the old React UI, the Metric Explorer fuzzy search results use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without escaping, and heatmap cell tooltips interpolate le label values without sanitization. With Prometheus v3.x defaulting to UTF-8 metric and label name validation, characters like \u003c, \u003e, and \" are now valid in metric names and labels. An attacker who can inject metrics via a compromised scrape target, remote write, or OTLP receiver endpoint can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the Graph UI, potentially enabling configuration exfiltration, data deletion, or Prometheus shutdown depending on enabled flags. This issue has been fixed in versions 3.5.2 and 3.11.2. If developers are unable to immediately update, the following workarounds are recommended: ensure that the remote write receiver (--web.enable-remote-write-receiver) and the OTLP receiver (--web.enable-otlp-receiver) are not exposed to untrusted sources; verify that all scrape targets are trusted and not under attacker control; avoid enabling admin or mutating API endpoints (e.g., --web.enable-admin-api or --web.enable-lifecycle) in environments where untrusted data may be ingested; and refrain from clicking untrusted links, particularly those containing functions such as label_replace, as they may generate poisoned label names and values."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44903",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series databas ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. From 2.49.0 to before 3.5.3 and 3.11.3, in the Prometheus server's legacy web UI (enabled via the command-line flag --enable-feature=old-ui), the histogram heatmap chart view does not escape le label values when inserting them into the HTML for use as axis tick mark labels. An attacker who can inject crafted metrics can execute JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the heatmap chart UI. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44903",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44903\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/prometheus/prometheus\nFixed Version: 0.311.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-44903](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44903)\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. From 2.49.0 to before 3.5.3 and 3.11.3, in the Prometheus server's legacy web UI (enabled via the command-line flag --enable-feature=old-ui), the histogram heatmap chart view does not escape le label values when inserting them into the HTML for use as axis tick mark labels. An attacker who can inject crafted metrics can execute JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the heatmap chart UI. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44903**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/prometheus/prometheus|0.311.3|[CVE-2026-44903](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44903)|\n\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. From 2.49.0 to before 3.5.3 and 3.11.3, in the Prometheus server's legacy web UI (enabled via the command-line flag --enable-feature=old-ui), the histogram heatmap chart view does not escape le label values when inserting them into the HTML for use as axis tick mark labels. An attacker who can inject crafted metrics can execute JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the heatmap chart UI. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47913",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
